; ============================================================
;  ARMOR MAG POUCHES - the carry boxes
;
;  A box is a container you carry, and it only takes one sort of thing.
;
;  IT HAS TWO SIZES AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME NUMBER:
;
;    inv_grid_width / height   how much room it takes up in your bag
;    amp_box_w / amp_box_h     how much room there is inside it
;
;  They were both "two by two out, five by five in" while there were
;  three boxes. There are eight now, from a 2x1 food container to a 2x3
;  armour case, so both are written out per section.
;
;  THE ICON RECTS ARE PRINTED BY art/mkboxdds.py and copied from its
;  output. A slot on that sheet is permanent - inv_grid_x/y is in every
;  save that holds the box - so a new box takes the next free slot
;  rather than the one it looks like it belongs in.
;
;  WHY THESE SECTIONS LOOK LIKE THE RIGS
;  -------------------------------------
;  Because they ARE the rig sections with three fields changed. The rig
;  template is af_magpouch_s from the installed magazine mod, and it is
;  copied field for field - including class = II_ATTCH, which is what
;  the items that DO appear in the debug spawner carry. Everything that
;  is not identity is the template's own number. See the note at the top
;  of mod_system_amp_rigs.ltx; it applies here word for word.
;
;  WHAT MAKES A BOX A BOX
;  ----------------------
;    amp_box       = true      the marker, read the same way amp_rig is
;    amp_box_takes = <family>  which rules in items\amp_boxes.ltx apply
;    amp_box_w / h             the grid inside it
;    amp_box_kg                how much it will carry, in kilograms
;    amp_box_stack             how many of one thing share one square
;
;  THE SQUARES SAY WHAT FITS; THE KILOGRAMS SAY WHAT YOU CAN LIFT. A
;  box that is five by five inside and free to carry is a bag of
;  holding - twenty-five squares of ammunition is most of a rucksack,
;  in something you can also put in your rucksack. Ten is generous and
;  still means something.
;
;  The stack ceiling is separate because it is about SPACE, not weight:
;  twenty-five squares is not many if every bandage takes one. Only
;  identical things stack - same wear, same uses, same rounds.
;
;  NO use_condition. A rig wears out and is mended; a box is a box. It
;  has no bar on its icon and nothing can tear.
;
;  dont_stack stops the inventory merging two of them into one cell.
;  Boxes are not interchangeable once they have something in them - each
;  one's contents are filed against ITS object id - so two boxes must
;  stay two objects.
;
;  THEY ARE NOT ON THE RIG SHEET ANY MORE:
;
;    "make that so rigs and boxes dont use the same file for the
;     textures"
;
;  ui\ui_amp_boxes is theirs, on a 7 x 7 unit pitch, so slot (col,row)
;  is inv_grid_x = col*7, inv_grid_y = row*7 and the rect inside it is
;  whatever that box's shape is.
;
;  TWO KEYS THAT ONLY SOME OF THEM CARRY:
;
;    amp_box_snd = metal       what the box sounds like when its
;                = plastic    window opens and closes. Unmarked means
;                = cloth      plastic; the wallet says cloth, and the
;                = chest      ammo cases say chest - a latched lid,
;                             shipped with the mod as sounds\amp\.
;
;    amp_box_noweight = true   room is the only limit. The armour case.
;    amp_box_pick = fill       the pile is ORDERED, and which one comes
;               = cond         out depends on how you take it: letting
;                              go hands you the best, the split key
;                              hands you the worst. `fill` is rounds in
;                              a magazine, `cond` is how worn a part is.
; ============================================================

